;;; Syntax probe — config.
;;;
;;; A `(config …)` block, which every view has to render as data rather
;;; than as a fact. The flag is a real one — the fixture is about the *form*,
;;; and an unknown flag would make the file a load-negative, which is what
;;; `examples/broken/load/config_unknown_flag.ein` is for.
;;;
;;; One of the eighteen node-kind fixtures. As corpus entries they are
;;; rendered under every parse view and every op, and each rendering is
;;; digested by `corpus_shapes.md5`, so a change to how any of these
;;; shapes is drawn moves a digest. They exist because no *puzzle*
;;; contains these shapes.

(config :lattice-order-seed 3)
